{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.ReebGaugeGroup","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.ReebGaugeGroup","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Subgroup.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ReebGaugeGroup.embedding_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ReebGaugeGroup.embedding_injective","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/reeb-gauge-group.lean#L36-L36","doc":"The embedding is injective (norm-one condition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ReebGaugeGroup.embedding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ReebGaugeGroup.embedding","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/reeb-gauge-group.lean#L34-L34","doc":"The carrier embeds into the multiplicative group of R. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ReebGaugeGroup.groupInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ReebGaugeGroup.groupInst","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/reeb-gauge-group.lean#L32-L32","doc":"Group structure on the carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ReebGaugeGroup.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ReebGaugeGroup.carrier","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/reeb-gauge-group.lean#L30-L30","doc":"The underlying group of norm-one elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ReebGaugeGroup.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ReebGaugeGroup.mk","kind":"ctor","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/reeb-gauge-group.lean#L28-L28","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ReebGaugeGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ReebGaugeGroup","kind":"structure","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/reeb-gauge-group.lean#L22-L36","doc":"**Reeb gauge group** `U₁(R)`: the maximal torus of the gauge group,\nviewed as an R-group scheme.  Over ℂ this recovers U(1) = {e^{iθ}}.\n\nAbstractly, it is the group of norm-one elements in the rank-one\nweight lattice, equivalently `Aut⊗(τ|_⟨V⟩)`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:glossary-reeb-gauge-group","label":"rem:glossary-reeb-gauge-group","md":"quantum-observable-universe/glossary/glossary-reeb-gauge-group.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}